%% One deployment's configuration on one operator machine (~/.baas/deployments/<name>.yaml).
%% The name is the file's, given once (or derived by setup on a machine with none); the region is found from the bucket.
%% A CI job never has a file: it takes the deployment from its operator role (see baas-ci-e2e).
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> NoConfig
    NoConfig --> Operator: --deployment P config sync --operator-aws-profile p<br/>(proves p assumes P-role-operator, then writes region + profile)<br/>or admin deployment setup (the deployer profile is the source)
    NoConfig --> Adopted: --deployment P config sync<br/>(no profile: the default chain is the source)
    Adopted --> Operator: config set --operator-aws-profile
    Operator --> Operator: config set (preferences)
    Operator --> [*]: admin deployment teardown here<br/>(deletes deployments/P.yaml)
    Operator --> Orphaned: [elsewhere] admin deployment teardown
    Orphaned --> Operator: [elsewhere] setup, same region<br/>(no re-sync needed)
    Orphaned --> Adopted: [elsewhere] setup in another region,<br/>then --deployment P config sync
    Orphaned: Orphaned<br/>the deployment and its data are gone<br/>every command fails until a setup
